<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding the distance and displacement of a forest ranger as an application of vectors in real life</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A forest ranger starts at a base station and travels \({@d1@}\) km due North to a lookout tower. From the tower, the ranger then travels \({@d2@}\) km due East to reach a remote campsite.</p>

[[jsxgraph width="400px" height="400px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-2, 10, 10, -2], 
    axis: true,
    showCopyright: false
});

var n = {#d1#};
var e = {#d2#};

// Origin (Base Station)
var p1 = board.create('point', [0, 0], {name: 'Base', fixed: true});
// Lookout Tower
var p2 = board.create('point', [0, n], {name: 'Tower', color: 'blue'});
// Campsite
var p3 = board.create('point', [e, n], {name: 'Camp', color: 'green'});

// Path segments (Vectors)
board.create('arrow', [p1, p2], {strokeColor: 'blue', strokeWidth: 3});
board.create('arrow', [p2, p3], {strokeColor: 'green', strokeWidth: 3});

// Resultant Displacement
board.create('arrow', [p1, p3], {strokeColor: 'red', strokeWidth: 2, dash: 2});
[[/jsxgraph]]

<p>Using the knowledge of vectors, calculate:</p>
<ol>
    <li>The total distance travelled by the ranger. [[input:ans1]] km [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</li>
    <li>The magnitude of the ranger's total displacement from the base station. [[input:ans2]] km [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]
</li>
</ol>
<p><i>(Round your displacement to 2 decimal places.)</i></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3> Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To differentiate between scalar and vector quantities:</p>

<p><b>(a) Total Distance (Scalar Sum)</b></p>
<p>Distance only considers the path length regardless of direction:</p>
<p>
\(\begin{align}
\text{Distance} &= d_1 + d_2 \\
&= {@d1@} + {@d2@} \\
&= {@ta1@} \text{ km}
\end{align}\)
</p>

<p><b>(b) Displacement (Vector Magnitude)</b></p>
<p>Displacement is the straight-line distance from the start point to the end point. Since the movements are perpendicular (North and East), we use Pythagoras:</p>
<p>
\(\begin{align}
|\vec{s}| &= \sqrt{d_{\text{North}}^2 + d_{\text{East}}^2} \\
&= \sqrt{{@d1@}^2 + {@d2@}^2} \\
&= \sqrt{{@d1^2 + d2^2@}} \\
&= {@ta2@} \text{ km}
\end{align}\)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
